# Project Custom Layer (forever-optimizations)

This file is **yours**. `awe-setup` creates it once and never touches it again — not on re-run, not on upgrade. Rules 00/10/20 are refreshed by setup; this layer is where your project accumulates its own wisdom over time.

Use it for things like:

- **Conventions** — "migrations live in `db/migrate`, never edit old ones", "all API errors use the `AppError` shape".
- **Gotchas** — "the staging bucket is shared, never run integration tests against it", "`FlakyTest.checkout` needs `--runInBand`".
- **Patterns discovered mid-ticket** — when a review finding teaches something general, write the lesson here so every future agent run benefits.
- **House style** — naming, folder layout, preferred libraries (so agents stop proposing alternatives).

Tips:

- Keep it short and high-signal; long rule files dilute attention.
- Split into additional `.mdc` files with `globs:` frontmatter when a rule only applies to part of the tree (e.g. `globs: ["src/api/**"]`).
- Delete entries that stop being true. Stale rules are worse than no rules.
